---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Browse Camera Lenses – Camera Central"
  description="Explore camera lenses by system and find the right fit for your setup."
>
  <div class="w-full max-w-5xl mx-auto space-y-8">
    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Lenses</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">
        Browse lenses by system
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-gray-600">
        Explore lens ecosystems and learn what fits your camera body. Start with Canon for now,
        and more systems can be added as Camera Central grows.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <a
        href="/lenses/canon-rf"
        class="group rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
        style="cursor:pointer;"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Canon Mirrorless</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Canon RF / RF-S</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Browse native lenses for Canon RF mount cameras like the R50, R10, R7, R8, R6 Mark II,
          and R5.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <li>RF full-frame lenses</li>
          <li>RF-S APS-C lenses</li>
          <li>Good for modern Canon mirrorless systems</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
          Explore RF lenses →
        </span>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/lenses/canon-ef"
        class="group rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50"
        style="cursor:pointer;"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-500">Canon DSLR / Adapted Options</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Canon EF / EF-S</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Browse Canon DSLR lenses, including full-frame EF and APS-C EF-S options. Many of these
          can also be adapted to Canon RF bodies.
        </p>

        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <li>EF full-frame DSLR lenses</li>
          <li>EF-S APS-C DSLR lenses</li>
          <li>Good for legacy Canon systems and adapter setups</li>
        </ul>

        <span class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-gray-900">
          Explore EF lenses →
        </span>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">How lens compatibility works</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
        Not every lens fits every camera body. Some lenses fit directly, while others need an
        adapter or may force the camera into crop mode. Camera Central will keep highlighting that
        so beginners do not accidentally buy the wrong lens.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>